### Android app testing via ADB reverse (wired device / emulator) ###
#
# The Android app's ApiConfig.BASE_URL points to http://localhost:8080/api,
# i.e. the Spring Boot backend running on the developer's machine.
#
# When testing the app on a physical device connected by USB (wired), run the
# following command ONCE in a terminal while the device is connected (USB
# debugging enabled):
#
#     adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080
#
# This forwards localhost:8080 from the phone to localhost:8080 on this PC, so
# the app reaches the backend without hardcoding an IP or configuring Wi-Fi.
#
# Note: the same command is also required when testing on an Android Studio
# emulator as long as BASE_URL uses localhost — inside the emulator "localhost"
# is the emulator itself, not your PC. (Alternative for emulators only: point
# BASE_URL at http://10.0.2.2:8080/api, the alias that reaches the host PC,
# then adb reverse is not needed — but physical devices then need a LAN IP.)
#
# Rerun the adb reverse command after reconnecting the device or restarting
# the emulator, since the forwarding is cleared when the connection drops.